{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>This is what HaShem spoke, saying: בקרבי אקדש.</b> And where did He speak? ״וְנוֹעַדְתִּי שָׁמָּה לִבְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל וְנִקְדַּשְׁתִּי בִכְבוֹדִי״ etc. Another interpretation: where did He speak? ״וְגַם הַכֹּהֲנִים הַנִּגָּשִׁים אֶל ה' יִתְקַדָּשׁוּ פֶּן יִפְרֹץ בָּם ה'״ — in the case of the high priests who draw near to me to serve me, I wish to be sanctified, and my name and my service shall not be profaned, as it is written: ״וְהַכֹּהֵן הַגָּדוֹל מֵאֶחָיו״ etc. ״וּבְגָדָיו לֹא יִפְרֹם וּמִן הַמִּקְדָּשׁ לֹא יֵצֵא וְלֹא יְחַלֵּל אֵת מִקְדַּשׁ אֱלֹהָיו״ — thus if he went out he profanes it. And there is no earlier and later in the Torah." "<b>ועל פני כל העם אכבד.</b> He sees his sons dying and sets aside his mourning for the sake of my service." "<b>וידם אהרן.</b> As we find in Ezekiel: ״הֵאָנֵק דֹּם אֵבֶל מֵתִים אַל תַּעַשׂ״ — so too here, <b>וידם אהרן</b> from what he had wanted to mourn."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {0 "The phrase 'הא אם יצא חלל' is rendered hyper-literally; the logical connection to the preceding citation is terse and possibly elliptical in the source."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:11:04.537384381Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}